      "extract": "The simplest known deﬁnition of the Jones polynomial is the Kauﬀman bracket [8], which in this paper will be denoted by ⟨·⟩A1 and will be called the A1 bracket. The A1 bracket is given by the following recursive rules: | 〉A1 = −(q 1/2+q -1/2)| 〉A1 | 〉A1 = −q 1/4| 〉A1 − q -1/4| 〉A1 The goal of this part of the paper is to derive deﬁnitions of the following three variants of the Jones polynomial: Theorem 1.1. There is",
      "extractCut": true
