      "extract": "Topological preliminaries By a planar graph we mean a ﬁnite combinatorial graph which is embedded in the sphere S2. We allow planar graphs to have edges which go in a circle and have no vertices, as well as a multiple edges between vertices and vertices connected to themselves. A face of a planar graph is a connected component of the complement of the graph. When interpreting the illustrations of planar graphs in",
