      "extract": "Invariants of colored ribbon graphs We begin with a summary of Reshetikhin and Turaev’s deﬁnition and some basic properties. We review some of the theory of ﬁnite-dimensional left modules, or representations, of a Hopf algebra H. If we have two representations V and W, the tensor product V ⊗W is also a representation by the coalgebra structure of H. There is a trivial representation I such that I ⊗V ∼= V ⊗I ∼= V",
