      "extract": "Questions open to the author The coeﬃcients a, b, c, d1, d2, e1, and e2 in the deﬁnition of the G2 bracket, as well as their analogues for the A2 and C2 brackets, are all Laurent polynomials in q with either nonpositive or nonnegative integer coeﬃcients. This is a coincidence which cannot be explained by the freedom in choosing the parameter q. The coeﬃcients could be complicated rational or even algebraic functions",
